{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytInsertMaxTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SytInsertMaxTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTInsertMax","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingBijection"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.insertMax_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.insertMax_injective","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytInsertMaxTransport.lean#L114-L136","doc":"`insertMax` is injective for a fixed corner: it changes only the cell `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.swapTableau_insertMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.swapTableau_insertMax","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytInsertMaxTransport.lean#L87-L112","doc":"`insertMax` intertwines the partial `s_k`-action: swapping then inserting is inserting then\nswapping.  With `axialDist_insertMax` and `swapAdmissible_insertMax_iff` this is everything\n`genMat`'s entry rules read, so the seminormal matrix of a generator that avoids the top entry has\nthe same entries on the block as it does downstairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.swapAdmissible_insertMax_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.swapAdmissible_insertMax_iff","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytInsertMaxTransport.lean#L78-L85","doc":"`SwapAdmissible` is defined from `cellOf`, so it too transfers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.axialDist_insertMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.axialDist_insertMax","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytInsertMaxTransport.lean#L69-L76","doc":"Hence `insertMax` preserves the axial distance at any pair of smaller entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.cellOf_insertMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.cellOf_insertMax","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytInsertMaxTransport.lean#L51-L67","doc":"`insertMax` does not move the cell of any smaller entry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}